-- Passage rg5-comparing-texts-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('aba426a3-e8ac-591a-a5bf-09b601eb3e1a', 'rg5-comparing-texts-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Team Comes First$q$, $q$Text 1: The Last Shot (a sports story)

With ten seconds left, the Hawks were down by one point. Jasmine had the ball. She had scored eighteen points already, and the crowd was chanting her name. She wanted to take the winning shot herself.

Two defenders rushed at her. Out of the corner of her eye, Jasmine saw her teammate Noor standing alone near the basket. Noor had not scored all game.

Jasmine passed. Noor caught the ball, took a breath and made the shot. The buzzer sounded. The Hawks had won! The team lifted Noor onto their shoulders, and Jasmine cheered the loudest of all.

Text 2: Anchor Leg (a sports story)

Tomas was the fastest swimmer on the relay team, so he always swam the last leg. Before the big meet, Coach Ibarra gave the last spot to Wen instead. Tomas was angry. "We will lose," he muttered.

During warmups, he noticed Wen's hands shaking. Tomas swam over. "Just touch the wall hard," he told her. "Don't look at the other lanes."

The team finished second, not first. But Wen swam her best time ever, and Tomas was the first to give her a high five. On the bus home, he realized he felt prouder of Wen's swim than of any race he had won alone.$q$, 'draft')
