   $q$Which theme do both tales share?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Older animals always know more than younger ones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"only-one-text"},{"text":"You should take everything you can while you can.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Being patient can lead to a bigger reward later.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Talking animals can never be trusted to tell the truth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Being patient can lead to a bigger reward later.$q$, $q$The crow finds sweet mangoes after waiting, and Kwame catches a huge fish after letting the small one go. The wise old crow appears only in Text 1, so that idea is not shared.$q$, 'draft', 'd6a69aac-0bba-5872-9324-113523ecba23')
